## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of the Trie (prefix tree) data structure, covering insert, delete, and prefix-query operations with proper edge case handling.

## Key Concepts

- **Trie node structure**: Each node stores 26 child pointers, an end-of-word flag, and a pass-through counter for efficient prefix queries
- **Safe deletion**: Decrement counts along the path and only unmark end-of-word when the word actually exists
- **Prefix query**: Return the count at the prefix's last node in O(length of prefix) time
- **Duplicate handling**: Adding the same word twice increments the counter twice; deleting decrements twice, effectively removing one occurrence

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Array(26).fill(null);
    this.isEndOfWord = false;
    this.count = 0;
  }
}

class Trie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  add(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) {
        node.children[index] = new TrieNode();
      }
      node = node.children[index];
      node.count++;
    }
    node.isEndOfWord = true;
  }

  delete(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) return;
      node = node.children[index];
      node.count--;
    }
    node.isEndOfWord = false;
  }

  countPrefix(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      const index = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[index]) return 0;
      node = node.children[index];
    }
    return node.count;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Duplicates are common in real data and inputs are often skewed. A 3-way partition quicksort directly handles the middle bucket of equal keys, avoiding repeated swaps of equal elements and preventing degeneracy.

## Key Concepts

- 3-way partitioning (Dutch national flag style) for handling duplicates
- Pivot selection strategies (median-of-three to reduce worst-case risk)
- Introsort/hybrid switching to guarantee worst-case bounds
- In-place sorting with O(log n) recursion depth

## Code Example

```javascript
function threeWayQuicksort(a, lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1) {
  while (lo < hi) {
    let lt = lo, i = lo + 1, gt = hi;
    const pivot = a[lo];
    while (i <= gt) {
      if (a[i] < pivot) { [a[lt], a[i]] = [a[i], a[lt]]; lt++; i++; }
      else if (a[i] > pivot) { [a[i], a[gt]] = [a[gt], a[i]]; gt--; }
      else { i++; }
    }
    threeWayQuicksort(a, lo, lt - 1);
    lo = gt; // tail recursion on the right side
  }
  return a;
}
```

